From c8734b4492a81a136b66845a2dc0c39626ce407c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:45:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(2d): place typed text as single-line engraving strokes

A typed string becomes a profile of tool-centreline strokes on the top
face of a setup's stock. It is the first slice of #2679.

- camcraft-geometry: stroke_text, our own single-line stroke font
  (capital letters, digits, the space and - _ . : / # + = ( )) and its
  layout into polylines and into SketchData on the layer "text".
- camcraft-app: the undoable InsertText command and the MCP tool
  insert_text. The text is the same Sketch entity as a DXF profile, so
  MoveSketch, DeleteEntity, get_job and the project file work on it.
- Refused by name: an empty text, a character with no glyph (a
  lower-case letter is not changed to a capital), a size outside the
  limits, a placement that is not finite, a setup with no stock, a name
  in use.

The toolpath is not in this change: generation from profile chains is
refused on main until #1869. docs/decisions/2679-engrave-typed-text.md
records why the font is a stroke font and what was dropped.

Refs #2679

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
